    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d715-a1-a2-a1">

                <pb facs="1098" n="1002" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg1002"/>

                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Port of—</hi>District of—,<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ss:</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#flush">No. 14.—25851.</p>
                <p>I, John F. Patterson, of the city, county, and State of New York, do solemnly
                    swear, according to the best of my knowledge and belief, that the ship or vessel
                    called the <pb facs="1099" n="1003" xml:id="pg1003"/> Virginius, of New York, is
                    of the burthen 441 84/100 of tons, and was formerly the steamer Virgin, and sold
                    by order and on account of United States Government, as per copy of register No.
                    106, issued at the port of New Orleans 23d June, 1866. Now canceled. Property
                    changed.</p>
                <p>That my present place of abode or residence is New York, and that I am a citizen
                    of the United States, and the true and only owner of the said ship or vessel,
                    and there is no subject or citizen of any foreign prince or state directly or
                    indirectly, by way of trust, confidence, or otherwise, interested therein, or in
                    the profits or issues thereof, I and that F. E. Shepperd is the present master
                    or commander of the said ship or vessel.</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN F. PATTERSON.</signed></closer>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Sworn to <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1870-09-26">this 26th day of September, 1870</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>W. A. MORRIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Deputy
                        Collector.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
